<template>
    <div id="app">
        <piko:partial is="layout"
            server.title="Ricotta Be Kidding Me Lasagna"
            server.current-page="recipes">

            <article class="page-section page-section--reading">
                <piko:img class="recipe-hero" src="@/lib/images/recipe-ricotta-be-kidding-lasagna.jpg" alt="Ricotta Be Kidding Me Lasagna"></piko:img>

                <header class="mt-lg">
                    <h1 class="recipe-title">Ricotta Be Kidding Me Lasagna</h1>
                    <p class="recipe-pun">You ricotta be kidding me, three cheese layers!</p>

                    <div class="recipe-meta-row tag-row">
                        <span class="tag">Ricotta + Parmesan + Mozzarella</span>
                        <span class="tag">90 mins</span>
                        <span class="tag">Medium</span>
                        <span class="tag">8 servings</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="recipe-actions">
                        <m3e-split-button variant="filled" p-on:click="saveRecipe">
                            Save recipe
                            <m3e-menu-item slot="menu" p-on:select="addToMealPlan">Add to meal plan</m3e-menu-item>
                            <m3e-menu-item slot="menu" p-on:select="shareRecipe">Share recipe</m3e-menu-item>
                            <m3e-menu-item slot="menu" p-on:select="printRecipe">Print</m3e-menu-item>
                        </m3e-split-button>

                        <m3e-tooltip text="Add to favourites">
                            <m3e-icon-button toggle aria-label="Add to favourites">
                                <piko:svg src="@/lib/icons/favourite.svg" fill="currentColor" width="24" height="24"></piko:svg>
                            </m3e-icon-button>
                        </m3e-tooltip>

                        <m3e-tooltip text="Squeak peek: cooking tips">
                            <m3e-icon-button aria-label="Show cooking tips" p-on:click="openTips">
                                <piko:svg src="@/lib/icons/info.svg" fill="currentColor" width="24" height="24"></piko:svg>
                            </m3e-icon-button>
                        </m3e-tooltip>

                        <label class="switch-field">
                            <m3e-switch p-on:change="toggleUnits" aria-label="Use imperial measurements"></m3e-switch>
                            <span p-ref="unitLabel">Metric</span>
                        </label>
                    </div>
                </header>

                <m3e-tabs class="recipe-tabs" p-on:change="selectPanel">
                    <m3e-tab active>Ingredients</m3e-tab>
                    <m3e-tab>Method</m3e-tab>
                    <m3e-tab>Nutrition</m3e-tab>
                    <m3e-tab>Reviews (6)</m3e-tab>
                </m3e-tabs>

                <!-- Ingredients -->
                <section class="recipe-panel" p-ref="panel0" aria-label="Ingredients">
                    <div class="panel-header">
                        <h2 class="subsection-title">Ingredients</h2>
                        <div class="servings-control">
                            <span id="servings-label">Servings</span>
                            <m3e-slider class="servings-slider"
                                        discrete
                                        min="1"
                                        max="12"
                                        value="8"
                                        step="1"
                                        aria-labelledby="servings-label"
                                        p-on:change="changeServings"></m3e-slider>
                            <strong p-ref="servingsValue">8</strong>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div p-ref="ingredients">
                        <m3e-list>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="12">12</span> dried lasagna sheets</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="500" data-unit="g">500g</span> ricotta cheese</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="100" data-unit="g">100g</span> parmesan, finely grated</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="250" data-unit="g">250g</span> mozzarella, sliced or grated</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="500" data-unit="g">500g</span> beef mince</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="2">2</span> tins (400g each) chopped tomatoes</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="1">1</span> large onion, finely diced</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="3">3</span> cloves garlic, minced</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="1">1</span> large carrot, finely diced</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="2">2</span> sticks celery, finely diced</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="50" data-unit="g">50g</span> butter</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="50" data-unit="g">50g</span> plain flour</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="600" data-unit="ml">600ml</span> whole milk</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">A pinch of freshly grated nutmeg</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="1" data-unit="tsp">1 tsp</span> dried oregano</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">A handful of fresh basil leaves</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">Salt, to taste</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient">Freshly ground black pepper, to taste</span></m3e-list-item>
                            <m3e-list-item><span class="ingredient"><span class="qty" data-base="2" data-unit="tbsp">2 tbsp</span> olive oil</span></m3e-list-item>
                        </m3e-list>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Method -->
                <section class="recipe-panel" p-ref="panel1" aria-label="Method" hidden>
                    <h2 class="subsection-title">Method</h2>
                    <ol class="step-list">
                        <li>Heat the olive oil in a large pan over medium heat. Add the onion, carrot, and celery, cooking for 5 minutes until softened. Add the garlic and cook for another minute. Then add the beef mince and brown it well, breaking it up with a wooden spoon. This is honest, wholesome work. You&rsquo;re building layers of flavour. You&rsquo;re also about to build actual layers. Stir in the tinned tomatoes, oregano, salt, and pepper. Simmer for 30 minutes.</li>
                        <li>While the bolognese simmers, make the b&eacute;chamel. Melt butter, stir in flour, cook for 1 minute. Gradually add the milk, whisking continuously. Cook for 5&ndash;7 minutes until thick and velvety. Season with nutmeg. Now, taste the parmesan to check it&rsquo;s suitable for the dish. Have another taste to confirm. Actually, that&rsquo;s really good parmesan. One more piece. Okay, stop. You need that for the lasagna.</li>
                        <li>In a bowl, mix the ricotta with half the grated parmesan. Season with salt and pepper. Stir it until smooth. Taste it. Oh no. Oh no, that&rsquo;s incredible. This is just the filling and it&rsquo;s already better than most things you&rsquo;ve eaten this week. Stay focused.</li>
                        <li>Preheat the oven to 180&deg;C. Now begins the sacred ritual of layering. Bolognese on the bottom, then lasagna sheets, then ricotta, then b&eacute;chamel. Repeat three times. This is your masterwork. Each layer is a chapter in the story of cheese. Try not to eat the ricotta mix between layers. We believe in you. Mostly.</li>
                        <li>Scatter the mozzarella and remaining parmesan over the top. Step back. Behold what you have built. A monument to cheese. An edible cathedral. If the parmesan pile looks a bit thin, it&rsquo;s because you ate some in step 2 and you know it.</li>
                        <li>Bake for 40 minutes until golden and bubbling. If it browns too quickly, cover with foil. We&rsquo;re going for &ldquo;golden perfection,&rdquo; not &ldquo;charcoal surprise.&rdquo;</li>
                        <li>Remove from the oven and rest for 10 minutes. Yes, ten whole minutes. We know the smell is making you feral. We know you&rsquo;re hovering over it with a spatula like a wolf. But resting lets the layers set so your slices look neat and not like a beautiful cheesy landslide. Garnish with fresh basil. Serve. Accept applause.</li>
                    </ol>
                </section>

                <!-- Nutrition -->
                <section class="recipe-panel" p-ref="panel2" aria-label="Nutrition" hidden>
                    <h2 class="subsection-title">Nutrition (per serving)</h2>
